212
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:22,098
This is Creed.

213
00:11:22,182 --> 00:11:24,934
And he is in charge of something.

214
00:11:25,018 --> 00:11:26,060
Right? That is correct.

215
00:11:26,144 --> 00:11:28,062
Say hi to the kids. Hi, kids.

216
00:11:29,022 --> 00:11:31,649
Have you ever seen a foot with four toes?

217
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:34,668
What are you doing? Stop it! Stop it! Just... No, no, no, no, no!

218
00:11:34,736 --> 00:11:35,987
Would you cut it out?

219
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:38,156
What is your problem? The hair covers it up mostly.

220
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:41,284
No, no, no, we're not gonna see the four-toed Creed, okay?

221
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:43,220
You know, there's something interesting about me

222
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:47,081
that you might want to know. I used to be the star of a kids' show.

223
00:11:47,165 --> 00:11:49,083
- No way! - It's true. I did.

224
00:11:49,167 --> 00:11:51,044
You serious? I am totally serious.

225
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:54,631
There was a show called <i>Fundle Bundle</i> and I was the star.

226
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:56,354
That doesn't sound like a show. It's true.

227
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:58,134
I can prove it. I can prove it. Watch this.

228
00:11:58,218 --> 00:12:00,303
Ryan! Can you come here a second?

229
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:04,766
I would like you to go to my mother's house in Dickson City.

230
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:05,975
And if she is at the pool,

231
00:12:06,059 --> 00:12:07,894
the back kitchen window should be unlocked.

232
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,580
I want you to boost yourself up. All right.

233
00:12:09,604 --> 00:12:12,124
I want you to go down to the basement. In the basement is a tape

234
00:12:12,148 --> 00:12:13,358
labeled <i>"Fundle Bundle."</i>

235
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,441
I want you to grab it. I want you to get my guitar.

236
00:12:15,485 --> 00:12:16,837
Right. Okay. I want you to get a tambourine.

237
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:18,255
Do you know how to play the tambourine?

238
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:20,341
I'm already getting the pizzas from Brunetti's, so...

239
00:12:20,365 --> 00:12:22,200
You know, I can go with him. No!

240
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:25,411
I will go. Okay. Thank you, Ryan.

241
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,413
Good attitude. Hottest in the office.

242
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:30,250
All right. Now, what kind of pizza do you like?

243
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,133
<i>I don't get why parents are always complaining</i>

244
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:34,420
<i>about how tough it is to raise kids.</i>

245
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:35,964
<i>You joke around with them,</i>

246
00:12:36,047 --> 00:12:38,258
<i>you give them pizza, you give them candy,</i>

247
00:12:38,341 --> 00:12:41,344
<i>you let them live their lives. They're adults, for God's sake.</i>

248
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:44,764
I am going to give you a little blast from the past

